From 55b7b83d0aa3fa0dd42b6c8b8bf050e1a5fd4368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:55:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(post): probing hooks for the Tormach PathPilot post
 (G38.2)

Voice onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult in tormach.cps in
LinuxCNC words, from the LinuxCNC G-code reference and Tormach's
PathPilot post-processor guidelines: each touch is G38.2 (the control
halts on no contact), the trip is read from #5061-#5063 (the WCS the G38
ran in), the back-off is incremental (G91 ... G90), a deviation past the
tolerance shows (MSG, ...) and ends the program (M2) inside a uniquely
numbered o-word if/endif, and the work offset is set with G10 L20 from
the current position #5420-#5422 minus the deviation (exact in program
units, unlike G10 L2 from #5221..). Without an offset to set the program
stops for the operator (MSG + M0). A section stating 0 rpm (a touch
probe) starts no spindle, writes no belt note and turns on no coolant.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/probe_tormach.rs with face / edge / outside
corner / bore / boss goldens on the 770MX (inch) and a metric bore under
golden/nc/tormach/, and probe_op.rs the_tormach_post_probes_the_op_with_g38_2.

Fixes #362

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
