+
+/// LinuxCNC evaluates arithmetic only inside brackets: a parameter
+/// assignment is `#n=#m` or `#n=[expr]`, never a bare `#n=#m-0.7874`
+/// (PathPilot Hub 2.14.4 refused that with "Bad character '-' used"),
+/// and no `--` / `+-` is ever written.
+fn assignments_are_bracketed(prog: &str) {
+    for l in prog.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with('#')) {
+        let Some((_, rhs)) = l.split_once('=') else { panic!("an assignment without '=': {l}") };
+        let plain = rhs.starts_with('#') && rhs[1..].chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_digit());
+        assert!(plain || (rhs.starts_with('[') && rhs.ends_with(']')), "unbracketed expression: {l}");
+        assert!(!rhs.contains("--") && !rhs.contains("+-"), "a doubled sign: {l}");
+    }
+}

From e2291de8af3f307b7ed76d79b8d910d226f4580c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:40:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(post): probe programs report the measured deviation
 on the control

The Tormach PathPilot post writes (DEBUG, PROBE <axis> ERROR #19n) per
probed axis after its tolerance test and before the G10 L20 offset write
(or the measure-only MSG/M0 stop): LinuxCNC's DEBUG comment shows in the
status display without stopping and substitutes #n. The Fanuc-family
post records that macro B has no non-stopping display (#3000 alarms,
#3006 stops) and writes nothing. Sinumerik (MSG) and Heidenhain (none
confirmed) are recorded for when their probe hooks land.

Fixes #575

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
