From d3217facf4863761c2112f6ad16039cf823f8ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:27:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(post): the probe report names its unit

The Tormach PathPilot probe report now ends with the program's unit:
(DEBUG, PROBE <axis> ERROR #19n MM) in a G21 program and ... IN) in a
G20 one, from the same `inch` flag that writes G20/G21 - asked for after
the real 770MX run, where an inch deviation read like a mm value. The
Tormach probe goldens change only in that word; probe_report pins IN on
the inch 770MX and MM on a metric (no machine file) program.

Refs #575

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
